  "facts": [
    "The Colle di Tenda Road Tunnel, opened in 1882, was the world’s longest road tunnel at 3,182 meters, engineered by Giovanni Delfino and built entirely within the Kingdom of Italy before 1947.",
    "In 2012, a dual‑tunnel upgrade began, adding a 6.50‑meter carriageway for France‑bound traffic while widening the original tube for Italy, a project that cost €255 million and faced fraud investigations.",
    "After landslides in 2020 closed the old tunnel, the new tube reopened in June 2025, offering alternating one‑way traffic from 06:00 to 21:00 on weekends and split shifts on weekdays."
